1 0 0 1 58 545 Tm (Haanel writes from the early twentieth-century New Thought tradition. He uses terms such) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 530 Tm (as Universal Mind, subconscious mind, solar plexus, vibration, Law of Attraction, spirit) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 515 Tm (and Silence within his own philosophical and metaphysical framework.) Tj
0.14 0.20 0.28 rg
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 492 Tm (Those terms should not be silently translated into modern neuroscience. For example,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 477 Tm (Haanel's account of the solar plexus as the centre of subconscious activity is his) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 462 Tm (historical model; it is not the current anatomical understanding of the nervous system.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 447 Tm (Likewise, his claims that thought directly creates external conditions are philosophical) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 432 Tm (and spiritual claims, not established scientific laws.) Tj
0.14 0.20 0.28 rg
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 409 Tm (A modern reader can study the text respectfully without pretending that every claim has) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 394 Tm (been scientifically demonstrated. The distinction is important throughout this guide.) Tj
