1 0 0 1 58 522 Tm (Haanel uses the conscious and subconscious mind as explanatory categories. He associates) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 507 Tm (conscious activity with reasoning and will, and subconscious activity with habit, memory) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 492 Tm (and automatic processes. Modern psychology also recognises both deliberate and automatic) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 477 Tm (mental processes, but that does not validate every detail of Haanel's model.) Tj
0.14 0.20 0.28 rg
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 454 Tm (Haanel also gives the solar plexus a central role in subconscious activity and discusses) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 439 Tm (the vagus nerve in his account of the nervous system. Modern anatomy describes the vagus) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 424 Tm (nerve as a major nerve of the autonomic nervous system, connecting the brainstem with) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 409 Tm (organs including the heart, lungs and digestive system. The solar plexus is a network of) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 394 Tm (nerves in the abdomen; it is not recognised as the anatomical seat of the subconscious) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 379 Tm (mind.) Tj
0.14 0.20 0.28 rg
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 356 Tm (There is a real relationship between mental states and bodily processes. But there is no) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 341 Tm (established evidence that affirmations travel through the vagus nerve to the solar plexus) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 326 Tm (and become subconscious commands. The historical theory and modern anatomical account) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 311 Tm (should not be conflated.) Tj
